From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 05:04:07 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: share one test harness across the driver tests

Every KosmicKrisp test carried its own copy of the same checks.  39 C and
Objective-C tests defined CHECK in three shapes (two boolean messages and a
VkResult form), nineteen of them the same LOAD_I and LOAD_D, 27 C++ tests
the same require() and load<>(), and the line-planner helper its own
KK_TEST_CHECK.  tests/kk_test.h now holds one boolean CHECK, one VK_CHECK and
the C and C++ loaders; the VkResult-form tests and the one CHECK_VK use
VK_CHECK.  Every check still names its expression and aborts in every build,
and the C++ require() still exits with status 1.

The 46 tests that drive a device also each created an instance, found the
physical device and its graphics queue family, read the memory properties,
created a device with one queue and loaded the same device entry points,
and most repeated the same shader-module, command-pool and submit-and-wait
code.  struct kk_test_device now holds that setup: kk_test_create_instance()
and kk_test_create_device() create the instance and the device,
KK_LOAD_DEVICE_FUNCTIONS() loads the 40 core entry points that ten or more
tests call, and kk_test_memory_type(), kk_test_shader_module(),
kk_test_command_buffer() and kk_test_submit_and_wait() replace the copies.
Each test still enables exactly the features and extensions it did, and the
C++ tests that looped over every physical device take the one an Apple host
exposes.  Tests about the life of a command pool, fence or timeline keep
their own pool and submission code, which is what they test.

The buffers, image allocations and image views the tests create come
from kk_test_buffer(), kk_test_image_memory() and kk_test_image_view():
a buffer with its own memory and an optional mapping, the memory of an
image the test described itself, and a view of one mip level.  A
resource that chains anything onto its buffer, allocation or view,
shares an allocation with another, or builds an invalid view on purpose
keeps its own code.  The ten whole-library tests that built their own
instance, device and command buffer use the fixture's as well.

The Meson stanzas become loops over tables that give each test its name,
timeout and whatever else sets it apart - sources, dependencies, arguments
or environment: the Vulkan-level C++ tests, the whole-library internal and
GPU tests, the public-API and Metal-bridge tests, the header-only helper and
NIR-to-MSL compiler tests, and the tests that build driver sources, NIR
lowering passes or the vertex-buffer lowering into themselves.  Every
environment a test sets starts from one kk_test_env.  Near-copies become
cases of one executable, each case run in its own process: the dynamically
uniform TES sampler test of the uniform one, the geometry and tessellation
draw-size tests of test_draw_size, and the layered draw sequence test of the
layered draw routes test.  The point-clip test reads the polygon-point
fragment shader it had duplicated byte for byte.  Test names, timeouts and
environments are unchanged.

One tests/generate-shaders.sh rebuilds the SPIR-V headers of every shader
directory, or of those it is given, in place of 26 per-directory generate.sh
scripts, and runs the script xfb_builtin_shaders keeps for the three
variants of its one shader.

