+/* KK_WORKAROUND_18: a render command encoder that already ran one draw drops
+ * most of the primitives of a later draw that selects a different
+ * render_target_array_index, so the workaround has to see every Metal draw
+ * that selects a layer, however the application reaches it.  Each route runs
+ * in a fresh process because only the first affected pass of a process loses
+ * primitives:
  *
+ *   sequence    one draw call per layer with a vertex-shader layer: one point
+ *               per texel into layer 0 of a two-layer attachment, then one
+ *               point per texel of its first 16 rows into layer 1;
  *   multi_draw  one vkCmdDrawMultiEXT whose two entries select layers 0 and 1
  *               through gl_DrawID, so the second is a later Metal draw of the
  *               same call;
  *   geometry    one draw call per layer, with the layer written by a geometry
  *               shader rather than the vertex shader.
  *
- * Every texel of every layer must carry the value its own layer's draw
- * writes.
+ * Every texel each draw covers must carry the value its own layer's draw
+ * writes.  The attachment size, the layered point draws and the DONT_CARE
+ * load op all matter: without the workaround a later draw loses its leading
+ * points, but a CLEAR load op on the same pass renders correctly.  The short
+ * second draw of the sequence also catches the rest of the workaround: a
+ * restarted encoder ordered behind the first only by a barrier still loses
+ * leading 1984-point batches of it in most fresh processes, unless the queue
