- * two-layer attachment and then one point per texel of its first 16 rows into
- * layer 1, one draw per layer, and require every texel each draw covers to
- * carry the value its own layer's draw writes.
- *
- * The attachment size, the layered point draws and the DONT_CARE load op all
- * matter: without the workaround the second draw loses its leading points,
- * but a CLEAR load op on the same pass renders correctly. The short second
- * draw also catches the rest of the workaround: a restarted encoder ordered
- * behind the first only by a barrier still loses leading 1984-point batches
- * of it in most fresh processes, unless the queue finishes the first encoder
- * before starting the second.
